{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3978","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3978","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3978\",\"parent_revision\":\"0e60ec10d7ee8c26a8f53b899b6f3f36e7c0dec9\",\"root_revision\":\"259dcd5c63f7c347ed6b65d8dd5d44c356f7adbf5504c5b0e655ea29877c66f5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: in-progress\\nadded: 2026-09-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA REST 403 for the primary rate limit ('API rate limit exceeded', RateLimitExceededException, often without a Retry-After header) is classified NON_RETRYABLE by sync_state._classify_github_exception. Sync then goes OFFLINE and MCP responses report retryable: false while the limit is only temporary. Found by Codex on #3968 (PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6mbw5i); the behaviour predates #3968.\\n\\nUser-provided context: classify RateLimitExceededException as retryable before the generic 403 rule, and take the delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:01:42.736351Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Primary-quota 403 rate limit is classified non-retryable\\nDate: 2026-09-28\\nGoal: A primary-quota 403 (RateLimitExceededException / exhausted x-ratelimit-remaining) classifies as RETRYABLE with a delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of the misclassification (sync_state._classify_github_exception, 403 branch) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Existing rate-limit detection helper to reuse (gh_client._is_rate_limited) and the import-direction constraint between gh_client and sync_state | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. How a retry delay flows from the classifier to the scheduler / MCP retryable field | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Shape of GitHub primary-limit 403 responses (headers present, message text) | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0cef272c426927e6e7efb3fddfed1987a5a250d20ed60d7e3ea7fc016832bbce\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXUwMFg\",\"fields\":{\"source\":\"Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\",\"files\":\"\",\"added\":\"2026-09-27\",\"status\":\"in-progress\",\"plan\":\"\",\"stack\":\"\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"2026-09-27\",\"topic\":\"\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"item_type\":\"Bug\"}}"}